<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:49:15 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>🔴 Macron orders plan to protect France critical infrastructure against 'Russian hybrid attacks'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-macron-orders-plan-to-protect-france-critical-infrastructure-against-russian-hybrid-attacks</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">ee1eb63a-b35b-11f1-af42-31fb72e0081a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:24:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron orders plan to protect France's critical infrastructure against 'Russian hybrid attacks'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-macron-orders-plan-to-protect-france-critical-infrastructure-against-russian-hybrid-attacks</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Friday said he had ordered measures to protect France's critical infrastructure and defence industry sites from "Russian hybrid attacks", adding that the threat from Moscow had intensified in recent weeks. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73761a32-b328-11f1-ad78-8bce42b8e305/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247415545627.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73761a32-b328-11f1-ad78-8bce42b8e305/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247415545627.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">af546d00-b35b-11f1-be79-451e5df98ed4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:23:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73761a32-b328-11f1-ad78-8bce42b8e305/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26247415545627.jpg">© Firas Abdullah via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Prized Aztec codex returns to Mexico on loan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-prized-aztec-codex-returns-to-mexico-on-loan</link><description>
A cherished 16th-century Mexican manuscript that tells the history of the Aztecs in pictograms went on display Thursday in Mexico City, nearly two centuries after it was whisked off to France. France's National Library, which has maintained possession of it for over a century, loaned it to Mexico to commemorate 200 years of relations between the two countries, although Mexico is pushing for its permanent return.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c363502-b355-11f1-a991-a9fb07cae23b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-132319-132512-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c363502-b355-11f1-a991-a9fb07cae23b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-132319-132512-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">91e14b36-b355-11f1-a545-074438ab0286</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:44:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France’s Yellow Vests to return as fuel prices soar?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-france-s-yellow-vests-to-return-as-fuel-prices-soar</link><description>
Eight years after fuel taxes helped spark the Yellow Vest movement, calls for a return to the streets are gathering momentum in France amid soaring energy prices. Recent days have seen fishermen blockading ports and oil terminals in protest at price hikes, but they are far from the only group feeling the squeeze.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80e87670-b354-11f1-98dc-d16598924449/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-130633-130816-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80e87670-b354-11f1-98dc-d16598924449/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-130633-130816-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a9aabce-b354-11f1-9465-11d3a4957ba7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:43:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>How will rise of AI impact Africa?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-how-will-rise-of-ai-impact-africa</link><description>
The threat of catastrophic danger as artificial intelligence develops at high speed has sparked a global debate on how it should be regulated. And Africa is no exception. As governments and businesses look to harness the technology, concerns are growing over jobs, misinformation and the need for safeguards.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/729b7340-b34c-11f1-9dae-a9fb07cae23b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-225010-225200-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/729b7340-b34c-11f1-9dae-a9fb07cae23b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-225010-225200-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77cb50ce-b34c-11f1-bfc2-e1a679736603</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:06:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>The Cameroon civil society groups taking on gender-based violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-the-cameroon-civil-society-groups-taking-on-gender-based-violence</link><description>
August 2026 has been a particularly tragic month for women in Cameroon, as eight cases of femicides were recorded in eight days. These figures add to the sixty or so cases already recorded since the start of the year by the Ministry of Women's Empowerment and the Family. On the ground, associations are mobilising to provide legal and psychological support to families in a country where a complaint of domestic violence rarely leads to a conviction. Indira Ayuk, Richard and Giresse Ngaana report from Yaoundé.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b217d236-b34a-11f1-b52c-a9fb07cae23b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-224535-224731-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b217d236-b34a-11f1-b52c-a9fb07cae23b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-224535-224731-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b7474944-b34a-11f1-8b36-ad57f7ec4f5c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:54:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France’s Macron summons party leaders for talks on Mideast and Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-france-s-macron-summons-party-leaders-for-talks-on-mideast-and-ukraine</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron is meeting leaders of France’s political parties at the Elysée on Friday for talks on the wars in the Middle East and Ukraine and the consequences for the country’s security and energy amid soaring fuel prices.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f255e6da-b34a-11f1-b16b-d16598924449/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2261985286aad110da53a35-48649151.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f255e6da-b34a-11f1-b16b-d16598924449/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2261985286aad110da53a35-48649151.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1096a640-b349-11f1-ba7d-fdc6cf5f4d3f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:24:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Russian elections a ‘veneer of democracy’ with opposition barred from running</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russian-elections-a-veneer-of-democracy-with-opposition-barred-from-running</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Friday, September 18: Russia holds its first parliamentary elections since the Ukraine war. Since only parties loyal to Vladimir Putin are running, the elections are seen as nothing but a veneer of democracy. In sports: Zinedine Zidane will unveil his first selection as coach of the French football team. Brisbane 2032 Olympic and Paralympic organisers approve a croc-infested river to hold canoe and rowing events. Finally, the first new feline species in a century has been discovered.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f775775a-b329-11f1-9799-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-18T05-21-22-519Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f775775a-b329-11f1-9799-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-18T05-21-22-519Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1cec5602-b32a-11f1-a039-298075db8772</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:16:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Venezuela lifts block on some news sites as transition talks resume</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-venezuela-lifts-block-on-some-news-sites-as-transition-talks-resume</link><description>
Venezuela has unblocked some news sites that had been censored for years, its telecom regulator said Thursday, as US-backed political transition talks were set to resume. Digital rights group VE Sin Filtro verified access to 17 news sites through several internet providers. However, at least 188 websites remain blocked, it said, including 79 news outlets.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e14b54f4-b347-11f1-8398-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-101249-101419-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e14b54f4-b347-11f1-8398-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-101249-101419-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e6f7ac54-b347-11f1-8b8f-b57346b04ee2</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:04:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia votes in wartime election set to secure the Kremlin's power</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-russia-votes-in-wartime-election-set-to-secure-the-kremlin-s-power</link><description>
Voting got ⁠underway on Friday in a tightly controlled three-day parliamentary election in Russia which President Vladimir Putin has framed as a barometer of support for Russia's war in Ukraine. It is the first parliamentary election since Russia launched its full-scale war in Ukraine in February 2022, and most anti-war candidates have been excluded from the ballot.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e55eda88-b343-11f1-8d1a-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-101014-101158-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e55eda88-b343-11f1-8d1a-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-101014-101158-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb2d6de4-b343-11f1-b202-f5fe1e3a3d52</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:52:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Police move hundreds of migrants still in Ceuta off beaches in Spanish enclave</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-police-move-hundreds-of-migrants-still-in-ceuta-off-beaches-in-spanish-enclave</link><description>
Spanish police in Ceuta on Friday morning started moving hundreds of migrants from the beaches of the Spanish enclave to a new tented area. Several thousand migrants remain in Ceuta after tens of thousands of people crossed the border with Morocco in late July. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/836abfca-b345-11f1-a6a9-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C86X4R8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/836abfca-b345-11f1-a6a9-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C86X4R8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7bd2f7de-b343-11f1-8c0a-1560ea7fe23b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:51:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/836abfca-b345-11f1-a6a9-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C86X4R8.jpg">© Antonio Sempere, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UN mission says grounds to believe US committed war crimes in Iran</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-un-mission-says-grounds-to-believe-us-committed-war-crimes-in-iran</link><description>
A UN fact-finding mission on Iran said on Thursday it had reasonable grounds to believe the United States was behind two military strikes on a school and sports facility in Iran in February, and that these constituted war crimes. It also found that Iranian authorities committed crimes against humanity during their deadly crackdown on anti-government protests. France 24’s Kethevane Gorjestani takes a closer look at the report’s findings.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e8a3b6a-b342-11f1-bc0e-d16598924449/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-100356-100938-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e8a3b6a-b342-11f1-bc0e-d16598924449/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-100356-100938-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24389d36-b342-11f1-9b3d-47fc27d50ce3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:31:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘We cried the whole way’: Refugees flee Yemen fighting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-we-cried-the-whole-way-refugees-flee-yemen-fighting</link><description>
An estimated 125,000 people, including more than 57,000 children, have fled since hostilities erupted in July between the Iran-backed Houthi rebels, the Yemeni government and its ally Saudi Arabia, with the UN calling it one of the most rapid and volatile waves of displacement in Yemen in years. Thousands have even been making the dangerous crossing across the Bab el-Mandeb strait to Djibouti, many of them children, travelling in extreme heat, often without enough water.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc74c7dc-b340-11f1-84bf-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-100143-100326-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc74c7dc-b340-11f1-84bf-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-100143-100326-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e208126c-b340-11f1-ac0a-7f2a1854441f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:24:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia seizes assets of Swiss food giant Nestle and three French firms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-russia-seizes-assets-of-swiss-food-giant-nestle-and-three-french-firms</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin signed a decree on Thursday to transfer assets of Swiss food giant Nestle and three French groups to a company called LEV Management. Most Western companies quickly sold their Russian operations and holdings after Moscow launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine, and the Kremlin has since made it difficult for firms to leave the country. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/652a0772-b33c-11f1-b4cf-9f16a64db909/w:1024/p:16x9/000-97249KE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/652a0772-b33c-11f1-b4cf-9f16a64db909/w:1024/p:16x9/000-97249KE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8bcbe04c-b33e-11f1-85e4-bbc13793bae0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:11:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/652a0772-b33c-11f1-b4cf-9f16a64db909/w:1024/p:16x9/000-97249KE.jpg">© Hector Retamal, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Far-right politician Éric Zemmour joins 2027 French presidential race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-far-right-politician-%C3%A9ric-zemmour-joins-2027-french-presidential-race</link><description>
French far-right politician Éric Zemmour said on Friday that he would run in next year's presidential election, joining far-right candidate Marine Le Pen, who was runner-up to President Emmanuel Macron in the last two elections. Zemmour is campaigning on a crackdown on immigration, including a plan to expel unemployed foreigners even if they are legal residents. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/23bd41de-b33a-11f1-afa9-2538446acac2/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26008389563206.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/23bd41de-b33a-11f1-afa9-2538446acac2/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26008389563206.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e6bcd08-b33a-11f1-b960-e76b244d1c83</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:06:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/23bd41de-b33a-11f1-afa9-2538446acac2/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26008389563206.jpg">© Emma Da Silva, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>Fear and broken families: Inside a Texas ICE detention centre</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260918-reporters-fear-and-broken-families-inside-a-texas-ice-detention-centre</link><description>
Since Donald Trump’s return to the White House in January 2025, migrant arrests have surged in the United States. More than 610,000 people have passed through detention centres run by Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), the federal immigration agency in under two years. The pace only continues to accelerate: in August 2026, nearly 51,000 arrests were made in a single month – a record for Trump’s second term. Who are the people being held in these centres? What are their living conditions like? And how is Trump’s mass deportation policy upending the lives of families settled in the United States? In this report, Valérie Defert and Pierrick Laurent investigate the issue in Texas – the heart of the new US immigration detention system.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d097924c-b29f-11f1-a6dc-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-texas-FR-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d097924c-b29f-11f1-a6dc-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-texas-FR-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf0933dc-b2b2-11f1-b5fe-cfee4b0c2fc9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 08:26:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Pierrick LEURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Election without meaningful competition': Russia’s results won't measure support for Putin or war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/election-without-meaningful-competition-russia-s-results-won-t-measure-support-for-putin-or-war</link><description>
Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. According to Roos, Russia’s parliamentary election is revealing because of what the electoral process can still tell us about the political system Vladimir Putin has constructed. In the absence of any meaningful competition, and anti-war opposition excluded, Roos argues that the most revealing signals may lie elsewhere: in turnout, the timing of voting, the performance of the remaining parties, and the Kremlin’s effort to frame participation itself as evidence of national unity.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00975aa6-b334-11f1-820a-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-080339-081115-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00975aa6-b334-11f1-820a-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-080339-081115-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06833098-b334-11f1-ad64-2f09393885d6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 08:14:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French PM vows to cut public spending by €54 billion to reduce deficit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-french-pm-vows-to-cut-public-spending-by-%E2%82%AC54-billion-to-reduce-deficit</link><description>
Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said on Thursday that France will cut public spending by €54 billion next year to reduce the country's deficit. The announcement comes seven months ahead of the country's presidential election, and the government is wary of a new wave of demonstrations with a jump in global oil prices sparking concerns over the rising cost of living. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b1526be-b330-11f1-abde-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26142371784910.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b1526be-b330-11f1-abde-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26142371784910.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">61b975d6-b32e-11f1-ab9e-b5bbc83805db</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 07:23:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b1526be-b330-11f1-abde-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26142371784910.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, AFP via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US approves $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 warplanes to Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260918-us-approves-24-3-billion-sale-of-48-f-35-warplanes-to-saudi-arabia</link><description>
The United States on Thursday said it had approved a $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 stealth warplanes to Saudi Arabia. Israel has previously voiced concerns about Riyadh buying F-35s, despite a push to normalise relations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5501408-b328-11f1-82fe-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T121806Z-145721001-RC2OFNAVWHNC-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5501408-b328-11f1-82fe-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T121806Z-145721001-RC2OFNAVWHNC-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e13024a-b328-11f1-b171-f5081862f07e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 06:29:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5501408-b328-11f1-82fe-1d1125ed9143/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T121806Z-145721001-RC2OFNAVWHNC-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg">© Claudia Greco, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Early voting begins in US midterms that could see Republicans lose control of Congress</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-early-voting-begins-in-us-midterms-that-could-see-republicans-lose-control-of-congress</link><description>
In-person early voting for the US midterm elections begins Friday, six weeks ahead of the final November 3 vote, which will determine whether Republicans will maintain their majority in the US House and Senate. Some of the main issues American voters are deciding on are how to navigate the cost-of-living crisis, the war in Iran and President Donald Trump’s aggressive immigration enforcement campaign. 
